# Brute Force / Password Spray Detection
# Detects multiple failed login attempts from a single source IP
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1110 - Brute Force
# Event Code: 4625 - An account failed to log on

index=main host=dc EventCode=4625
| stats count by src_ip
| where count > 5

# Description:
# This query counts failed logon events (EventCode 4625) grouped by source IP.
# A high number of failed attempts from a single IP indicates a brute force
# or password spraying attack.
#
# Lab Results: 105 failed login attempts from attacker IP 192.168.57.10
#
# Tuning recommendations:
# - Adjust the threshold (count > 5) based on your environment's baseline
# - Exclude known service accounts that may legitimately fail
# - Consider time windows (e.g., count > 5 in 1 hour vs. all time)
# - Whitelist trusted IP ranges (admin jump boxes, etc.)
#
# Alert threshold suggestion:
# - Trigger alert when count > 5 failed attempts in 1 minute from same src_ip
# - Escalate when count > 20 in 5 minutes
